WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.160
A dog eats a meal.

2
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.360
The food falls out of an opening in its neck before it reaches the stomach.

3
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.840
Yet the stomach pours out acid juice.

4
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.520
What told the stomach to start?

5
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.460
The answer came from Pavlov's laboratory in St. Petersburg.

6
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:29.233
Pavlov's laboratory opened the dog's esophagus at the neck, so swallowed food fell

7
00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:33.573
out. A gastric fistula let juice drain from the stomach.

8
00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:39.113
If juice flowed only when food touched the stomach, the dog should make none.

9
00:00:39.993 --> 00:00:44.953
Instead, after a delay of some minutes, abundant acid juice flowed.

10
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:49.997
Then both vagus nerves were cut.

11
00:00:50.897 --> 00:00:54.037
The vagus nerves connect the brainstem to the gut.

12
00:00:55.057 --> 00:00:57.477
Now eating no longer brought the juice.

13
00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:04.117
So in the dog, a nerve-driven cephalic phase exists, carried by the vagus.

14
00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:09.017
Sight, smell, taste and chewing of food trigger it.

15
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:15.237
It does not rule out later phases, which run once food is in the stomach or intestine.

16
00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:18.057
Later phases are partly chemical.

17
00:01:18.937 --> 00:01:23.977
A hormone is a substance released into the blood that acts on distant target cells.

18
00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:31.037
Gastrin is one. G cells in the stomach lining release gastrin when food, especially

19
00:01:31.037 --> 00:01:32.757
protein, is in the stomach.

20
00:01:33.857 --> 00:01:36.397
Gastrin makes the stomach secrete more acid.

21
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:42.427
Acid chyme then enters the duodenum, the first part of the small intestine.

22
00:01:43.207 --> 00:01:45.247
Its lining releases secretin.

23
00:01:46.207 --> 00:01:51.547
Secretin makes pancreatic duct cells secrete a bicarbonate-rich fluid, which

24
00:01:51.547 --> 00:01:53.407
neutralizes the stomach's acid.

25
00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.807
Fats and proteins in the duodenum bring out CCK.

26
00:01:58.587 --> 00:02:04.807
CCK drives the pancreas to release enzymes, and the gallbladder to contract and release bile.

27
00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.727
Nerves and hormones overlap.

28
00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:12.987
Healthy human volunteers were given CCK-8 at one dose.

29
00:02:14.147 --> 00:02:18.847
Atropine blocks the acetylcholine receptors that nerves use on many glands.

30
00:02:19.727 --> 00:02:24.707
With atropine, the pancreatic trypsin response fell by 84%.

31
00:02:24.707 --> 00:02:29.167
So in that test, much of the hormone's effect ran through nerves.

32
00:02:30.127 --> 00:02:35.687
Block one route, and the fraction that disappears estimates how much ran through it, under those conditions.
